All six features are implemented and verified. Here's what changed:

**`app/auth.py`** — `require_api_key` now reads the `X-API-Key` header, validates it against `VALID_API_KEYS`, and raises `HTTPException(401)` if missing or invalid.

**`app/main.py`** — Added the following endpoints and enhancements:
- **`GET /tasks`** — Optional query filters `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` (combinable), plus `page` (default 1) and `page_size` (default 20) pagination.
- **`POST /tasks`** — Requires auth via `Depends(require_api_key)`. Validates that `project_id` exists (404 if not). Auto-generates a unique integer ID (`max existing + 1`).
- **`PUT /tasks/{task_id}`** — Requires auth. Applies partial updates to `title`, `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to`. Returns 404 if not found.
- **`DELETE /tasks/{task_id}`** — Requires auth. Returns 204 on success, 404 if not found.

The module imports cleanly and all endpoints were exercised with `TestClient`: auth rejects missing/invalid keys with 401, filtering and pagination return correct slices, and create/update/delete behave as specified.
